docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_RE_RECORDING_AT_EVERY_TICK_STATIC_LAW_STATIONARY_LIGHT_CONE_BILAYER_LONG_RANGE_ORDER_GREEN_FUNCTION_RESPONSE_CONDITIONAL_ON_AN_EXCLUDED_CLAUSE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md:59:The static law, the pair law and the bilayer law are laws of the kind first written by Gibbs; the bilayer law with the sphere menu is the classical model of Heisenberg on that graph; the two-valued instance of the runner is the model of Ising. Asynchronous re-recording is the dynamics of Glauber for the static law. None of these names is used as authority.
