docs/GAUGE_WILSON_LOCAL_OBSERVABLE_FINITE_REGION_PW_APPROXIMATION_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-07.md:34:Let Lambda be any finite set of links of the infinite cubic lattice, with any chosen subset of its elementary plaquettes. On its full tensor L²(SU3) link carrier take H_Lambda=sum_e K_e+v sum_p(1-J_p), K_e=-(3/(2a))Delta_e, a>0,v>=0, J_p=ReTr(U_p)/3. The sum of v per face is scalar and does not affect Heisenberg evolution. Use centered interactions Phi_p=-v J_p, norm<=v. Every link belongs to at most4 plaquettes, each of4 links.
docs/INSTALLED_BACKGROUND_AUXILIARY_PREPARATION_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-10-15.md:439:During a control interval K moments need not be conserved. For example, the Heisenberg derivative satisfies  \(|d\langle K\rangle/dt|\le\|[G_j,K]\|\le2\beta\|G_j\|\). After controls stop, the same-K scalar moments are conserved under free K. The initial ideal baseline still has mean \(\operatorname{Tr}\rho H+c\), second moment \(\operatorname{Tr}\rho(H+cI)^2+\Delta\kappa\), and variance \(\operatorname{Var}_\rho(H)+\Delta\kappa\). Any covariance in a proposed physical decomposition is part of the full K-square; no term is discarded by identifying the compressed first moment with the complete generator.
docs/INTERACTING_CONTROLLER_HISTORY_APPLICATION_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-10-14.md:274:Perform `D_R` on the original enlarged source record only, tensor identity on `A,W`, all controller copies, dual rails, clock and reference. Because the record energies in (2) are diagonal, each `P_h` commutes with `H_ext`. It also commutes with every other bare energy term and with clock number. Thus the Heisenberg pinching fixes the bare Hamiltonian and the clock term, on every state including correlated states. This statement concerns original-record dephasing only; no dephasing is imposed on the fuel-copy record qubits, whose coherence is part of the supplied resource.
